  "comments": "<p>“With the 1979 issue, a general standardization of the coinage was launched. The portrait of the Queen was reduced to make it proportional to the diameter of the coin, regardless of denomination.” - Standard Charlton catalog Volume I</p><p><strong>1980 varieties:</strong> As a general rule, the style of the characters was examined and a more refined style was selected. - Standard Charlton catalog Volume I</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/67532593a1e22.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/67532593a1e22.jpg\"></a></p><p>“In 1981 the Royal Canadian Mint revamped its product line, adding a Proof finish to its offerings. Proof coins were issued on standard nickel plates.” - Charlton Standard Catalogue Volume I</p>",
